  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nAs the title implies having the \";\" character (in quotes as well) in the notif_from key causes the email to fallback to the machine hostname, thus preventing emails with a strict sender check\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\n  notif_from: \"ToS;DR %(app)s <matrix@tosdr.org>\"\r\n```\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/40178814/123369829-cf924f80-d57e-11eb-92f7-324aa67cc0d1.png)\r\n\r\nRemoving the semicolon fixes the issue.\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/40178814/123369871-e8026a00-d57e-11eb-9cf7-63cf540dc673.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n- Use a semicolon in the notif_from key\r\n- Send a test email\r\n\r\nIt should include the Semicolon as well.\r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\n\r\n- **Homeserver**: matrix.tosdr.org\r\n\r\nIf not matrix.org:\r\n\r\n<!--\r\n What version of Synapse is running?\r\n\r\nYou can find the Synapse version with this command:\r\n\r\n$ curl http://localhost:8008/_synapse/admin/v1/server_version\r\n\r\n(You may need to replace `localhost:8008` if Synapse is not configured to\r\nlisten on that port.)\r\n-->\r\n- **Version**: 1.31.1\r\n\r\n- **Install method**: Package Manager\r\n<!-- examples: package manager/git clone/pip  -->\r\n\r\n- **Platform**: Debian Buster (10) Not containerd, running on a dedicated server.\r\n\r\nCPU: AMD EPYC 7702 | 64 Cores with the average load being below 0.2 in general\r\nMemory: 64 GB DDR4 ECC RAM \r\n\r\nIdentity server is vector.im by default\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nTell us about the environment in which your homeserver is operating\r\ndistro, hardware, if it's running in a vm/container, etc.\r\n-->\r\n",
